adding 1 as

@lisp
(define zero (lambda (f) (lambda (x) x)))

(define (add-1 n)
  (lambda (f) (lambda (x) (f ((n f) x)))))
@end lisp

This representation is known as @newterm{Church numerals}, after its inventor,
Alonzo Church, the logician who invented the λ-calculus.

